i know that many of you would love to  become more productive and this  certainly applies to me as well but how  can you accomplish that one person from  the audience a couple of weeks ago sent  me a list from a service called filtered  where they analyzed what 100  productivity hacks and made a ranking  out of it so welcome to a new coffee  break here on my channel in this video i  will look into the top 10 productivity  hacks and i will give you my view  whether these are really effective or  not in the past i was sometimes a bit  skeptical about these productivity tips  i made a video about this in the past as  well linking it somewhere above here but  in the end of this video i will also  share one bonus tip a productivity tip  that really helped me in my life so stay  tuned and get into it the first  productivity tip i want to talk about is  time boxing time boxing means that you  look at your calendar you plan your week  or your month ahead and you schedule  some time into your calendar for things  that you really would like to accomplish  and i feel like this is especially  effective for things that are outside of  your regular work of course in your  regular work you know that you will need  to make the time for the things that  really matter but what is everything  that comes on top of that maybe you have  some side projects that you want to work  on maybe you have an exercise routine  that you want to prioritize make sure  that you block off this time in the  calendar and then be realistic we'll  even have enough time in the evenings on  the weekends to get this done make sure  to prioritize accordingly to get this  right next step is prioritization it is  of course essential that at work you  prioritize your tasks in the right way  so let me share three tips here these  are the rule of thumbs that i think  apply most of the time first focus on  things that need to move to other  people's desks so if someone else is  waiting for an input from you then this  person is able to progress the work by  him or herself prioritize this make sure  you get this through this other person's  desk as quickly as possible because then  you can also expect to get the result  back rather quickly of significantly  increasing productivity of the whole  team next do things first that usually  lead to some quick wins to some quick  results it's often quite frustrating if  you receive a project a task maybe from  your leadership and you do some things  first where you know that only in one or  two or three days of work you can  actually have something presentable in  your hand and of course then if your  leadership reaches out to you after one  day ask what you have done and you don't  really have anything you can show for  that's awful another idea and third to  prevent burnout especially when you're  sitting at your desk in the evening it's  already getting late  always ask yourself this specific piece  of work where you now feel like you need  to work on it right now  do you really need it for tomorrow is it  needed for your work day tomorrow and if  it's not do not work on it in the  evening next is the skill of saying no  especially juniors often feel like they  need to do everything that someone asked  them to do this is of course not really  a sustainable way of looking at your  work and if you struggle with this if  you struggle with saying no in such a  work environment i created a video in  the past where i also shared specific  tips on this situation i will link it  above fear feel free to check it out  next productivity tip is to move during  the day if you just sit in front of a  big screen from early morning until late  evening you will very likely get  depressed at some point your energy  level just naturally will go down what i  implemented for myself is now since a  couple of weeks almost every day from  monday to friday during lunch break i go  to the gym i signed up for a gym very  close to my office and then after i just  pick up something quick to eat during a  video conference or something like that  so that i do get some food in as well i  know this is not possible in every  single job but even at mckinsey during  my time in consulting i was able to at  least go for short walk maybe outside of  your clients building outside of your  home this does make a big difference  just to get some fresh air because  otherwise there might be days where you  don't even see the sun if in the early  morning you go into the office and then  off once you come back from the office  the sun has already gone down that's of  course not really a great environment to  work in next step control your devices  we all have experienced the situation  you receive a new email and then you  open slack and you see 500 messages on  slack that you look at your phone lots  of notifications on your phone how can  you even concentrate on this environment  how can you even get anything done in  this situation try to schedule some time  in your calendar maybe with time boxing  where you focus on working on your  emails to make sure that you really have  some time of uninterrupted work where  you can do some deep work done without  getting interrupted all the time by  these types of things if so far you took  any value out of this video please  destroy the like button and subscribe  for the youtube algorithm this would be  much appreciated and of course if you  have additional tips on productivity to  share leave me a comment in the comment  section but now let's continue next  productivity tip is to take short breaks  this is of course very much related to  the tip to move but of course if you are  the personality that just sits at his or  her desk and you really struggle to do  something else think about other tasks  incorporate a couple of these short  breaks frankly in an office environment  often this would be just a quick chat  with a colleague a little coffee break  in my humble opinion most people in  these environments don't really lack  these types of breaks but if you do make  sure to have the time for me again a big  game changer was the exercise the gym  time during the day that in itself is of  course a valuable breakaway next  productivity hack is to have an actively  managed to-do list either on a written  sheet or just in one of the many to-do  management apps that you can get on your  mobile phone on the pc on mac and so on  the main reason why this makes sense is  because it gives you peace of mind if  you don't write down all your to-do's  first it's very likely that you will  forget something and second you will  always feel stressed because suddenly  some to-do's pop up in your mind and you  don't really know whether this is  something to do now or maybe later you  are just afraid of forgetting it so  whenever you get a new task that you  need to get done just dump it in any of  these to do management programs because  then you know for sure that you will  have them all written down that you  won't forget anything and besides that  maybe that's also personality thing but  i feel like there's very few things  which are as satisfying as having a  sheet of paper in front of you or even  also one of these apps and being able to  just cross off to do's from that list  that personally always gives me a little  sense of accomplishment during the day a  little sense of self-efficacy so if you  feel in a similar way about that try it  out next productivity tip is to eat well  trust you all had the experience of  having had a very heavy lunch and then  in the afternoon just feeling down just  feeling like you lack any energy to get  anything productive done for the next  one two or even three hours that's of  course not great and probably also not  really healthy so avoid heavy lunches  and also be careful about all the snacks  that you eat during the day in some  companies in almost all meeting rooms  there are baskets of sweets of chocolate  and so on and it's just so easy to in  every other meeting eating a bit of this  chocolate so try to replace these snacks  with more healthy alternatives next  productivity tip is the two minute rule  this rule says that whenever you can get  a task done in two minutes do it now  don't postpone it to later if something  can get done in two minutes there's  really no reason to not taking action  right now don't even bother tracking it  in your to-do app just the fact that you  open your app or take your piece of  paper with your to-do's and you write it  down this alone will take one minute or  so right so just get it done right now  then it's finished and you're fine next  tip is to control your social media  consumption this is a problem that many  people have me included that you just  waste far too much time on all these  apps instagram facebook tech talk and so  on i think in most professional context  it's actually linkedin linkedin now  became this big social network where you  can read all these posts watch all these  videos and the mean thing is that for  many jobs you actually need linkedin as  one of the tools that you need for your  job frankly due to this reason i haven't  even found a good way of organizing  myself in this regard so if you have any  good tips to share on that just leave a  comment in the comment section  now finally i want to share the one  bonus advice that was not even present  in this list that i initially talked  about but i feel had a quite significant  impact on my life so many people are  using actually big headphones noise  cancelling headphones  in your work routine to just blend out  the noise and so on but in my humble  experience there is something that is  far more effective than all these noise  cancelling headphones and this is proper  earplug something like i have here in my  hand i start using these in university  especially during exams so it was always  allowed during exams to plug in ear  plugs like this and i feel like just the  fact alone that i used earplugs during  most of my exams helped me to improve my  grades by at least one or two points on  all of these exams at least for me  personally this was such a game changer  in how well i was able to concentrate  and even today whenever i want to have  focused quality work time of one hour  two hours or so we just want to sit in  front of my desk to get something done  there's nothing else that helps me as  much to concentrate as proper earplugs  again if you found this helpful please  leave a like i would very much  appreciate that big big thanks to all  the members of the channel for  supporting the work here at firm  learning my name is heinrich i release  weekly videos here on the channel see  you again next week until then and bye

